Theorem [\[ivanovolshanski\]](#ivanovolshanski){reference-type="ref" reference="ivanovolshanski"} implies in particular that the symbols $\varSigma_{\mu}$ factorize in higher degree, that is to say that for any partitions $\mu$ and $
u$, $$\varSigma_{\mu}\,\varSigma_{
u}=\varSigma_{\mu \sqcup 
u}+(	ext{terms of degree at most }|\mu|+|
u|-1).$$ The next paragraph is devoted to a better description of the products $\varSigma_{\mu}\,\varSigma_{
u}$; we shall rely on the formalism of partial permutations (*cf.* [@IK99]).
